ternal pressures, leading to its eventual dissolution and the rise of new states.","startYear",1293,"startMonth",0,"startDay","endYear",1527,"endMonth","endDay","startSignificance",0.9,"endSignificance",0.7,"imageUrl","https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Naval_flag_of_Majapahit_Kingdom.svg/330px-Naval_flag_of_Majapahit_Kingdom.svg.png","imageCredit","Image: Majapahit / Wikimedia Commons","sourceUrl","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Majapahit","cdnId","country",{"_32":83,"_84":85},"subjects",[77,78],"group",{"_32":74,"_75":76},"user",{"_30":71,"_72":73},"likes","liked",false,"6","username","HistOracle","Precolonial Southeast Asia","icon","GiTempleGate",{"_30":81,"_32":82},{"_30":79,"_32":80},"3","culture","2","politics","Indonesia","continent","Asia","2035","Kertanegara","person","A prominent ruler known for expanding the Singhasari kingdom and promoting trade and culture.","His reign ended with his death, marking a significant transition in the region's political landscape.",1268,1292,0.8,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/063_Main_Statue%2C_Joko_Dolog_%2839706345204%29.jpg/330px-063_Main_Statue%2C_Joko_Dolog_%2839706345204%29.jpg","Image: Kertanagara / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kertanegara",{"_32":83,"_84":85},[101,102],{"_32":74,"_75":76},{"_30":71,"_72":73},{"_30":81,"_32":82},{"_30":79,"_32":80},"1239","Sukhothai Kingdom","This period marked the rise of a significant kingdom in Southeast Asia, known for its contributions to art, culture, and governance.","The kingdom eventually declined, leading to the emergence of new powers in the region.",1238,1438,0.5,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Sukhotai_map.jpg/330px-Sukhotai_map.jpg","Image: Sukhothai Kingdom / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sukhothai_Kingdom",{"_32":119,"_84":85},[117,118],{"_32":74,"_75":76},{"_30":71,"_72":73},{"_30":81,"_32":82},{"_30":79,"_32":80},"Thailand","304","Angkor Wat","landmark","This temple complex is the largest religious monument in the world, originally constructed as a Hindu temple and later transformed into a Buddhist temple.","It remains a symbol of Cambodia and a significant site for both tourism and cultural identity.",1113,1150,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/20171126_Angkor_Wat_4712_DxO.jpg/330px-20171126_Angkor_Wat_4712_DxO.jpg","Jakub Hałun / Wikimedia Commons / CC BY-SA 4.0","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Angkor_Wat","images/53320d67ae477dc4412a22cb347d660c5c258c3c.webp",{"_32":139,"_84":85},[135,136],{"_32":74,"_75":76},{"_30":71,"_72":73},{"_30":79,"_32":80},{"_30":137,"_32":138},"7","religion","Cambodia","1604","Bali Kingdom","A historical kingdom known for its rich culture, arts, and Hindu influences.","The kingdom faced colonial pressures, leading to its eventual annexation by the Dutch.",914,1906,0.6,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Old_Flag_of_Bali.svg/330px-Old_Flag_of_Bali.svg.png","Image: Bali Kingdom / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bali_Kingdom",{"_32":83,"_84":85},[154,155],{"_32":74,"_75":76},{"_30":71,"_72":73},{"_30":79,"_32":80},{"_30":156,"_32":157},"9","art","2046","Pagan Kingdom","This period marks the rise of a powerful kingdom in Southeast Asia, known for its significant advancements in culture, religion, and architecture.","The kingdom eventually fell to the Mongol invasions and internal strife, leading to its decline and the emergence of successor states.",849,1297,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c0/Pagan_Empire_--_Sithu_II.PNG","Image: Pagan kingdom / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pagan_Kingdom",{"_32":173,"_84":85},[171,172],{"_32":74,"_75":76},{"_30":71,"_72":73},{"_30":81,"_32":82},{"_30":79,"_32":80},"Myanmar","2042","Jayavarman II","A prominent ruler who established the Khmer Empire, known for unifying various regions and promoting Hinduism as a state religion.","His reign marked the beginning of a powerful dynasty that would influence Southeast Asia for centuries.",802,850,"","Image: Jayavarman II / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jayavarman_II",{"_32":139,"_84":85},[187,188],{"_32":74,"_75":76},{"_30":71,"_72":73},{"_30":81,"_32":82},{"_30":137,"_32":138},"2041","Khmer Empire","This period marks the rise of a powerful kingdom in Southeast Asia, known for its impressive architectural achievements and cultural developments.","The decline of this period saw the fragmentation of the empire and the eventual loss of territory to neighboring states.",1431,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Map-of-southeast-asia_900_CE.svg/330px-Map-of-southeast-asia_900_CE.svg.png","Image: Khmer Empire / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khmer_Empire",{"_32":139,"_84":85},[201,202],{"_32":74,"_75":76},{"_30":71,"_72":73},{"_30":81,"_32":82},{"_30":79,"_32":80},"941","Borobudur","This magnificent Buddhist temple is the largest of its kind in the world, featuring a stunning array of relief panels and stupas. It is a masterpiece of ancient architecture and a significant pilgrimage site.","Borobudur has undergone extensive restoration and is now a UNESCO World Heritage Site, drawing visitors interested in its spiritual and historical significance.",800,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Pradaksina.jpg/330px-Pradaksina.jpg","Image: Borobudur / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Borobudur",{"_32":83,"_84":85},[215,216],{"_32":74,"_75":76},{"_30":71,"_72":73},{"_30":79,"_32":80},{"_30":137,"_32":138},"1596","Srivijaya","This powerful maritime empire was a center for trade and Buddhism in Southeast Asia, influencing regional cultures.","The empire eventually declined due to various factors, including competition from neighboring states and trade routes.",600,1200,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Srivijaya_Empire.svg/330px-Srivijaya_Empire.svg.png","Image: Srivijaya / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Srivijaya",{"_32":83,"_84":85},[231,232],{"_32":74,"_75":76},{"_30":137,"_72":230},"Kushim",{"_30":79,"_32":80},{"_30":233,"_32":234},"8","economic","943","Shwedagon Pagoda","This sacred Buddhist site is one of the most revered pagodas in Myanmar, known for its stunning golden stupa and rich history. It serves as a major pilgrimage site and a symbol of the country's spiritual heritage.","The pagoda continues to be a focal point for worship and cultural events, drawing visitors from around the world.","https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Shwedagon_Pagoda_2017.jpg/330px-Shwedagon_Pagoda_2017.jpg","Image: Shwedagon Pagoda / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shwedagon_Pagoda",{"_32":173,"_84":85},[246,247],{"_32":74,"_75":76},{"_30":71,"_72":73},{"_30":79,"_32":80},{"_30":137,"_32":138},"1606","Kingdom of Champa","An ancient kingdom known for its unique culture and trade networks along the South China Sea.","The kingdom was eventually absorbed into Vietnam, leading to the loss of its distinct identity.",192,1832,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Map-of-southeast-asia_1000_-_1100_CE.png/330px-Map-of-southeast-asia_1000_-_1100_CE.png","Image: Champa / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Champa",{"_32":263,"_84":85},[261,262],{"_32":74,"_75":76},{"_30":71,"_72":73},{"_30":79,"_32":80},{"_30":233,"_32":234},"Vietnam","2045","Funan Kingdom","This period marks the rise of a significant early civilization in Southeast Asia, known for its trade networks and cultural exchanges.","The period concluded as the kingdom fragmented, paving the way for the emergence of successor states in the region.",1,550,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Map_indianized_kingdoms_indochina.jpg/330px-Map_indianized_kingdoms_indochina.jpg","Image: Funan / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Funan",{"_32":139,"_84":85},[277,278],{"_32":74,"_75":76},{"_30":71,"_72":73},{"_30":79,"_32":80},{"_30":233,"_32":234},"2044","Dong Son Culture","This period is characterized by advanced bronze metallurgy and intricate artifacts, showcasing the cultural and artistic achievements of the society.","The period concluded as new influences and cultures began to emerge in the region, leading to significant changes in social and economic structures.",-1000,-100,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Dong_Son_axe.JPG/330px-Dong_Son_axe.JPG","Image: Đông Sơn culture / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dong_Son_culture",{"_32":263,"_84":85},[292],{"_32":74,"_75":76},{"_30":71,"_72":73},{"_30":79,"_32":80},"2043","Ban Chiang Culture","This culture is known for its advanced pottery, metalworking, and burial practices, reflecting a rich societal structure and artistic expression.","The culture gradually declined, influenced by external factors and the rise of new civilizations in the region.",-2000,-300,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Ban_Chiang_Museum_Excavation.JPG/330px-Ban_Chiang_Museum_Excavation.JPG","Image: Ban Chiang / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ban_Chiang",{"_32":119,"_84":85},[306],{"_32":74,"_75":76},{"_30":71,"_72":73},{"_30":79,"_32":80},[],"subject",[],[],"yearStart",-300000,"yearEnd",2025,"search","sortBy",true,31]
